Native review of Italian columns 010–018 is in `docs/i18n/global-plan/reviews/native/it-b.md`. Source files were not edited.

**Verdict:** columns **2/5** (guidance pack out of scope). The set is French legal prose in Italian words, with Spanish leftovers in 014 (`alega`) and blog register in 013–015. Wei Tseng is feminine except the 015 CTA (`un avvocato`). Strongest P1s: `persecuzioni` for prosecution, `processo clinico` for medical records, Korea put back in 011 against the English, `in qualunque momento a un avvocato`.

